Andi评分标准 数据收集 评分卡 AI工具 客户账户评估 GrowthX Fireflies transcripts Slack history Notion pages Scores GrowthX client accounts 1-5 on 5 dimensions using Andi''s rubric Compares scores to EM self-reported scores and flags misalignments Gathers data sequentially from Fireflies transcripts, Slack history, and Notion pages Extracts relevant signals from each data source before moving on Generates a compact scorecard (~1,000-1,500 words) for easy review account-health-scoring is a structured knowledge base skill that evaluates client accounts based on sequential data gathering from sources like Fireflies transcripts, Slack history, and Notion pages.');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Psqasim/personal-ai-employee/kafka-event-driven', 'community', 'Psqasim', 'personal-ai-employee', 'Psqasim/personal-ai-employee', 'kafka-event-driven', 1, 1, 42, '2026-03-02T06:26:54Z', '2026-03-06T07:20:38.457Z', 'b7599aee12d7f7489bd81eed8f703e8b2b2f7b844d83797209d564619f4a400a', '{"id":"Psqasim/personal-ai-employee/kafka-event-driven","name":"kafka-event-driven","description":{"en":"The kafka-event-driven skill enables developers to build scalable event-driven systems with Apache Kafka, supporting autonomous task execution and integration with various tools.","zh":"Kafka 事件驱动架构是一种分布式事件流平台，提供发布和订阅、存储和处理事件流的能力","ja":"Kafka イベント駆動アーキテクチャは、イベントストリームの公開とサブスクライブ、ストレージ、処理などの機能を提供する分散イベントストリーミングプラットフォームです","ko":"Kafka 이벤트 드리븐 아키텍처는 이벤트 스트림의 발행 및 구독, 저장, 처리 등의 기능을 제공하는 분산 이벤트 스트리밍 플랫폼입니다","es":"kafka-event-driven es una arquitectura de eventos que utiliza Apache Kafka para crear sistemas escalables y en tiempo real","fr":"kafka-event-driven est une architecture orientée événements qui utilise Apache Kafka pour créer des systèmes événementiels escalables et en temps réel","de":"kafka-event-driven ist eine Event-Driven-Architektur, die Apache Kafka verwendet, um skalierbare Echtzeit-Event-Systeme zu erstellen","pt":"O kafka-event-driven é uma habilidade que permite a criação de sistemas escaláveis de arquitetura orientada a eventos com Apache Kafka.","ru":"kafka-event-driven - это навык, который позволяет создавать масштабируемые системы архитектуры, основанной на событиях, с Apache Kafka.","ar":"kafka-event-driven هو مهارة يسمح بإنشاء أنظمة قابلة للتوسيع لهندسة مدفوعة بالأحداث مع Apache Kafka."},"seo":{"title":{"en":"kafka-event-driven: Event-Driven Architecture Setup Guide...","zh":"Kafka 事件驱动架构设置指南","ja":"Kafka イベント駆動アーキテクチャのベストプラクティス","ko":"Kafka 이벤트 드리븐 아키텍처 구축 가이드","es":"Guía de configuración de kafka-event-driven para arquitec...","fr":"Guide de mise en place de kafka-event-driven pour les arc...","de":"Einrichtungsleitfaden für kafka-event-driven-Event-Driven...","pt":"Guia de Configuração do kafka-event-driven: Arquitetura O...","ru":"Настройка kafka-event-driven: Руководство по архитектуре,...","ar":"دليل إعداد kafka-event-driven: هندسة مدفوعة بالأحداث"},"description":{"en":"Unlock scalable event-driven systems with Apache Kafka. Learn how to deploy and manage Kafka event streams with our expert guide and maximize your AI agent''s...","zh":"了解 Kafka 事件驱动架构的核心概念和关键组件，包括发布和订阅、存储和处理事件流","ja":"Kafka イベント駆動アーキテクチャのコアコンセプトとキーコンポーネントを学びます。イベントストリームの公開とサブスクライブ、ストレージ、処理など","ko":"Kafka 이벤트 드리븐 아키텍처의 핵심 개념과 주요 구성 요소를 알아보세요. 이벤트 스트림의 발행 및 구독, 저장, 처리 등","es":"Aprende a implementar kafka-event-driven con Apache Kafka para crear sistemas escalables de eventos en tiempo real","fr":"Découvrez comment mettre en œuvre kafka-event-driven avec Apache Kafka pour créer des systèmes événementiels escalables en temps réel","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie kafka-event-driven mit Apache Kafka implementieren, um skalierbare Echtzeit-Event-Systeme zu erstellen","pt":"Aprenda a configurar o kafka-event-driven para criar sistemas escaláveis de arquitetura orientada a eventos com Apache Kafka","ru":"Узнайте, как настроить kafka-event-driven для создания масштабируемых систем архитектуры, основанной на событиях, с Apache Kafka","ar":"تعلم كيفية إعداد kafka-event-driven لإنشاء أنظمة قابلة للتوسيع لهندسة مدفوعة بالأحداث مع Apache Kafka"},"definition":{"en":"kafka-event-driven is a skill that utilizes Apache Kafka for building event-driven architectures, enabling publish and subscribe, store, and process event streams in real-time or retrospectively.","zh":"Kafka 事件驱动架构是一种支持事件驱动系统构建的技术，具有发布和订阅、存储和处理事件流的能力","ja":"Kafka イベント駆動アーキテクチャは、イベント駆動システムを構築するための技術であり、イベントストリームの公開とサブスクライブ、ストレージ、処理などの機能を備えています","ko":"Kafka 이벤트 드리븐 아키텍처는 이벤트 드리븐 시스템을 구축하는 기술로, 이벤트 스트림의 발행 및 구독, 저장, 처리 등의 기능을 제공합니다","es":"kafka-event-driven es una arquitectura que permite la publicación y suscripción de eventos en tiempo real","fr":"kafka-event-driven est une architecture qui permet la publication et l''abonnement d''événements en temps réel","de":"kafka-event-driven ist eine Architektur, die die Veröffentlichung und das Abonnieren von Ereignissen in Echtzeit ermöglicht","pt":"O que é kafka-event-driven? É uma habilidade que permite a criação de sistemas de arquitetura orientada a eventos com Apache Kafka.","ru":"Что такое kafka-event-driven? Это навык, который позволяет создавать системы архитектуры, основанной на событиях, с Apache Kafka.","ar":"ما هو kafka-event-driven? هو مهارة يسمح بإنشاء أنظمة هندسة مدفوعة بالأحداث مع Apache Kafka."},"features":{"en":["Utilizes Apache Kafka for distributed event streaming","Supports publish and subscribe capabilities for event streams","Provides durable storage for event streams with fault tolerance","Enables real-time or retrospective processing of event streams","Integrates with tools like Claude Code and Obsidian for autonomous task execution","Includes human-in-the-loop approval workflow for enhanced control"],"zh":["支持事件驱动系统构建","提供发布和订阅、存储和处理事件流的能力","具有 Apache Kafka 分布式事件流平台","支持多步骤执行和人工审批工作流","集成了 Odoo 账务集成和 Claude 代码"],"ja":["イベント駆動システムを構築するための機能","イベントストリームの公開とサブスクライブ、ストレージ、処理などの機能","Apache Kafka 分散イベントストリーミングプラットフォームを搭載","マルチステップ実行と人間による承認ワークフローをサポート","Odoo 会計統合と Claude コードを統合"],"ko":["이벤트 드리븐 시스템 구축을 지원","이벤트 스트림의 발행 및 구독, 저장, 처리 등의 기능","Apache Kafka 분산 이벤트 스트리밍 플랫폼","다단계 실행 및 인간의 승인 워크플로를 지원","Odoo 계정 통합 및 Claude 코드를 통합"],"es":["Publicación y suscripción de eventos con Apache Kafka","Almacenamiento duradero de flujos de eventos","Procesamiento de flujos de eventos en tiempo real o retrospectivo","Integración con Odoo para la contabilidad","Automatización de correo electrónico y WhatsApp con Claude Code"],"fr":["Publication et abonnement d''événements avec Apache Kafka","Stockage durable de flux d''événements","Traitement de flux d''événements en temps réel ou rétrospectif","Intégration avec Odoo pour la comptabilité","Automatisation de courrier électronique et WhatsApp avec Claude Code"],"de":["Veröffentlichung und Abonnieren von Ereignissen mit Apache Kafka","Dauerhafter Speicher von Ereignisflüssen","Verarbeitung von Ereignisflüssen in Echtzeit oder retrospektiv","Integration mit Odoo für die Buchhaltung","Automatisierung von E-Mail und WhatsApp mit Claude Code"],"pt":["Publicação e assinatura de streams de eventos com Apache Kafka","Armazenamento durável de streams de eventos com tolerância a falhas","Processamento de streams de eventos em tempo real ou retrospectivo","Integração com Odoo para contabilidade","Automação de e-mail e WhatsApp com Claude Code + Obsidian"],"ru":["Публикация и подписка на потоки событий с Apache Kafka","Долговечное хранение потоков событий с устойчивостью к сбоям","Обработка потоков событий в реальном времени или ретроспективно","Интеграция с Odoo для учета","Автоматизация электронной почты и WhatsApp с Claude Code + Obsidian"],"ar":["نشر واشتراك في تدفقات الأحداث مع Apache Kafka","تخزين متين لتدفقات الأحداث مع تحمل الأعطال","معالجة تدفقات الأحداث في الوقت الفعلي أو بشكل متأخر","التكامل مع Odoo للحسابات","آلية بريد إلكتروني و WhatsApp مع Claude Code + Obsidian"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use kafka-event-driven","kafka-event-driven architecture","apache kafka event streaming","kafka-event-driven setup guide","kafka-event-driven vs rabbitmq","kafka-event-driven install","event-driven architecture with kafka","kafka-event-driven use cases","kafka-event-driven tutorial"],"zh":["Kafka 事件驱动架构","事件驱动系统","Apache Kafka","事件流平台","发布和订阅","存储和处理","Odoo 账务集成","Claude 代码"],"ja":["Kafka イベント駆動アーキテクチャ","イベント駆動システム","Apache Kafka","イベントストリーミングプラットフォーム","イベントストリームの公開とサブスクライブ","ストレージと処理","Odoo 会計統合","Claude コード"],"ko":["Kafka 이벤트 드리븐 아키텍처","이벤트 드리븐 시스템","Apache Kafka","이벤트 스트리밍 플랫폼","이벤트 스트림의 발행 및 구독","저장과 처리","Odoo 계정 통합","Claude 코드"],"es":["kafka-event-driven","arquitectura de eventos","Apache Kafka","event-driven architecture","desarrollo de software","integración de Odoo","automatización de correo electrónico","automatización de WhatsApp"],"fr":["kafka-event-driven","architecture orientée événements","Apache Kafka","event-driven architecture","développement de logiciels","intégration de Odoo","automatisation de courrier électronique","automatisation de WhatsApp"],"de":["kafka-event-driven","Event-Driven-Architektur","Apache Kafka","Ereignisgesteuerte Architektur","Softwareentwicklung","Odoo-Integration","E-Mail-Automatisierung","WhatsApp-Automatisierung"],"pt":["kafka-event-driven","arquitetura orientada a eventos","Apache Kafka","publicação de eventos","armazenamento de eventos","processamento de eventos","integração com Odoo","automação de e-mail","automação de WhatsApp"],"ru":["kafka-event-driven","архитектура, основанная на событиях","Apache Kafka","публикация событий","хранение событий","обработка событий","интеграция с Odoo","автоматизация электронной почты","автоматизация WhatsApp"],"ar":["kafka-event-driven","هندسة مدفوعة بالأحداث","Apache Kafka","نشر الأحداث","تخزين الأحداث","معالجة الأحداث","التكامل مع Odoo","آلية بريد إلكتروني","آلية WhatsApp"]}},"owner":"Psqasim","repo":"personal-ai-employee","repoPath":"Psqasim/personal-ai-employee","stars":1,"forks":1,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T06:26:54Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"kafka-event-driven","description":"Expert guidance for building event-driven architectures with Apache Kafka from hello-world prototypes to production-ready systems. Use when working with (1) Kafka producers and consumers, (2) Event streaming and stream processing with Kafka Streams, (3) Data integration with Kafka Connect, (4) Cluster setup and operations, (5) Production deployment and monitoring, (6) Schema management and data contracts, (7) Performance tuning and fault tolerance. Covers Java, Python, Node.js implementations.","bodyPreview":"# Apache Kafka Event-Driven Architecture\n\nBuild scalable event-driven systems with Apache Kafka - from local development to production deployment.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Event Streaming Platform\n\nKafka is a distributed event streaming platform with three core capabilities:\n\n1. **Publish and Subscribe** - Read and write streams of events (records)\n2. **Store** - Durably store event streams with fault tolerance\n3. **Process** - Process event streams in real-time or retrospectively\n\n### Key Compone","body":"# Apache Kafka Event-Driven Architecture\n\nBuild scalable event-driven systems with Apache Kafka - from local development to production deployment.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Event Streaming Platform\n\nKafka is a distributed event streaming platform with three core capabilities:\n\n1. **Publish and Subscribe** - Read and write streams of events (records)\n2. **Store** - Durably store event streams with fault tolerance\n3. **Process** - Process event streams in real-time or retrospectively\n\n### Key Components\n\n- **Producers** - Applications that publish events to topics\n- **Consumers** - Applications that subscribe to topics and process events\n- **Brokers** - Kafka servers that store and serve data\n- **Topics** - Named event streams organized into partitions\n- **Partitions** - Ordered, immutable sequences of events within a topic\n- **Consumer Groups** - Load-balanced consumption across multiple consumers\n- **Replication** - Data redundancy across brokers for fault tolerance\n\n## Quick Start Workflows\n\n### 1. Hello World - Local Setup\n\n**Start Kafka with Docker:**\n\n```bash\n# Pull and run Apache Kafka (includes KRaft - no Zookeeper needed)\ndocker pull apache/kafka:latest\ndocker run -p 9092:9092 apache/kafka:latest\n```\n\n**Create a topic:**\n\n```bash\n# Using Kafka CLI tools (if installed locally)\nbin/kafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \\\n  --create --topic hello-world \\\n  --partitions 3 --replication-factor 1\n\n# Using Docker\ndocker exec <container-id> /opt/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh \\\n  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \\\n  --create --topic hello-world \\\n  --partitions 3 --replication-factor 1\n```\n\n**Produce messages:**\n\n```bash\nbin/kafka-console-producer.sh --topic hello-world \\\n  --bootstrap-server localhost:9092\n```\n\n**Consume messages:**\n\n```bash\nbin/kafka-console-consumer.sh --topic hello-world \\\n  --from-beginning --bootstrap-server localhost:9092\n```\n\n### 2. Basic Producer (Java)\n\nSee `scripts/simple_producer.java` for a complete working example.\n\nKey configuration:\n\n```java\nProperties props = new Properties();\nprops.put(\"bootstrap.servers\", \"localhost:9092\");\nprops.put(\"key.serializer\", \"org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer\");\nprops.put(\"value.serializer\", \"org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer\");\nprops.put(\"acks\", \"all\"); // Wait for all replicas\nprops.put(\"retries\", 3); // Retry on transient errors\n\nKafkaProducer<String, String> producer = new KafkaProducer<>(props);\n```\n\n### 3. Basic Consumer (Java)\n\nSee `scripts/simple_consumer.java` for a complete working example.\n\nKey configuration:\n\n```java\nProperties props = new Properties();\nprops.put(\"bootstrap.servers\", \"localhost:9092\");\nprops.put(\"group.id\", \"my-consumer-group\");\nprops.put(\"key.deserializer\", \"org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringDeserializer\");\nprops.put(\"value.deserializer\", \"org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringDeserializer\");\nprops.put(\"enable.auto.commit\", \"false\"); // Manual offset management\nprops.put(\"auto.offset.reset\", \"earliest\"); // Start from beginning if no offset\n\nconsumer.subscribe(Collections.singletonList(\"my-topic\"));\n```\n\n## Advanced Patterns\n\n### Stream Processing with Kafka Streams\n\nFor stateful stream processing, windowing, joins, and aggregations, see:\n- **Reference**: [STREAMS_GUIDE.md](references/STREAMS_GUIDE.md)\n- **Script**: `scripts/word_count_streams.java`\n\n**When to use Kafka Streams:**\n- Real-time aggregations and analytics\n- Stream enrichment via joins (stream-stream, stream-table)\n- Windowed computations (tumbling, hopping, sliding)\n- Stateful transformations requiring local state stores\n\n### Data Integration with Kafka Connect\n\nFor integrating Kafka with databases, file systems, and external systems, see:\n- **Reference**: [CONNECT_GUIDE.md](references/CONNECT_GUIDE.md)\n- **Script**: `scripts/source_connector.java`\n\n**When to use Kafka Connect:**\n- Import data from databases (CDC patterns)\n- Export Kafka data to data warehouses\n- File-based integrations\n- Managed, scalable data pipelines without custom code\n\n### Transactions and Exactly-Once Semantics\n\nFor mission-critical applications requiring strong guarantees:\n\n```java\n// Producer configuration\nprops.put(\"enable.idempotence\", true);\nprops.put(\"transactional.id\", \"my-transactional-producer-1\");\n\nproducer.initTransactions();\n\ntry {\n    producer.beginTransaction();\n    producer.send(record1);\n    producer.send(record2);\n    producer.commitTransaction();\n} catch (Exception e) {\n    producer.abortTransaction();\n}\n```\n\nSee `scripts/transactional_producer.java` for complete implementation.\n\n## Production Deployment\n\n### Topic Configuration\n\n**Critical settings for production topics:**\n\n```bash\n# Create topic with production settings\nkafka-topics.sh --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --create \\\n  --topic production-events \\\n  --partitions 12 \\\n  --replication-factor 3 \\\n  --config min.insync.replicas=2 \\\n  --config retention.ms=604800000 \\  # 7 days\n  --config compression.type=lz4\n```\n\n**Key parameters:**\n- `partitions` - Parallelism (more = higher throughput)\n- `replication-factor` - Data redundancy (typically 3)\n- `min.insync.replicas` - Minimum replicas for writes (typically 2)\n- `retention.ms` - How long to keep data\n- `compression.type` - Compression algorithm (lz4, snappy, gzip, zstd)\n\n### Producer Configuration for Production\n\n```java\nprops.put(\"acks\", \"all\"); // Wait for all in-sync replicas\nprops.put(\"retries\", Integer.MAX_VALUE); // Retry indefinitely\nprops.put(\"max.in.flight.requests.per.connection\", 5);\nprops.put(\"enable.idempotence\", true); // Prevent duplicates\nprops.put(\"compression.type\", \"lz4\"); // Compress messages\nprops.put(\"batch.size\", 32768); // Batch size in bytes\nprops.put(\"linger.ms\", 10); // Wait time for batching\nprops.put(\"buffer.memory\", 67108864); // 64MB buffer\n```\n\n### Consumer Configuration for Production\n\n```java\nprops.put(\"enable.auto.commit\", false); // Manual commit control\nprops.put(\"max.poll.records\", 500); // Records per poll\nprops.put(\"max.poll.interval.ms\", 300000); // 5 minutes\nprops.put(\"session.timeout.ms\", 10000); // 10 seconds\nprops.put(\"heartbeat.interval.ms\", 3000); // 3 seconds\nprops.put(\"fetch.min.bytes\", 1024); // Minimum fetch size\nprops.put(\"fetch.max.wait.ms\", 500); // Max wait for fetch\n```\n\n### Monitoring and Observability\n\nSee [OPERATIONS_GUIDE.md](references/OPERATIONS_GUIDE.md) for comprehensive monitoring setup.\n\n**Key metrics to monitor:**\n- **Producer**: `record-send-rate`, `request-latency-avg`, `record-error-rate`\n- **Consumer**: `records-consumed-rate`, `records-lag-max`, `commit-latency-avg`\n- **Broker**: `under-replicated-partitions`, `offline-partitions-count`, `request-queue-size`\n\n### Security Configuration\n\nFor SSL/TLS and SASL authentication:\n\n```java\n// SSL configuration\nprops.put(\"security.protocol\", \"SSL\");\nprops.put(\"ssl.truststore.location\", \"/path/to/truststore.jks\");\nprops.put(\"ssl.truststore.password\", \"password\");\nprops.put(\"ssl.keystore.location\", \"/path/to/keystore.jks\");\nprops.put(\"ssl.keystore.password\", \"password\");\n\n// SASL/PLAIN configuration\nprops.put(\"security.protocol\", \"SASL_SSL\");\nprops.put(\"sasl.mechanism\", \"PLAIN\");\nprops.put(\"sasl.jaas.config\",\n    \"org.apache.kafka.common.security.plain.PlainLoginModule required \" +\n    \"username=\\\"admin\\\" password=\\\"secret\\\";\");\n```\n\n## Schema Management\n\nFor data contracts and schema evolution, see:\n- **Reference**: [SCHEMA_MANAGEMENT.md](references/SCHEMA_MANAGEMENT.md)\n\n**Schema Registry integration** (when using Confluent Schema Registry):\n\n```java\n// Avro producer\nprops.put(\"key.serializer\", \"org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer\");\nprops.put(\"value.serializer\", \"io.confluent.kafka.serializers.KafkaAvroSerializer\");\nprops.put(\"schema.registry.url\", \"http://localhost:8081\");\n```\n\n## Architecture Decision Guide\n\n### Choosing Number of Partitions\n\n**Factors to consider:**\n- Target throughput (more partitions = higher throughput)\n- Number of consumers in consumer group (max parallelism)\n- File handles per broker (more partitions = more file descriptors)\n\n**Rule of thumb:** Start with `max(target_throughput / partition_throughput, num_consumers)`\n\n### Consumer Group vs. Independent Consumers\n\n**Use Consumer Groups when:**\n- You need load balancing across multiple instances\n- Each message should be processed once by the group\n- You want automatic partition rebalancing\n\n**Use Independent Consumers when:**\n- Each consumer needs to process all messages\n- You need broadcast semantics\n- You want manual partition assignment\n\n### Kafka Streams vs. Custom Consumer\n\n**Use Kafka Streams when:**\n- You need stateful processing (aggregations, joins, windowing)\n- You want built-in fault tolerance and state management\n- Processing logic is complex with multiple transformations\n\n**Use Custom Consumer when:**\n- Simple message-by-message processing\n- Integration with non-Kafka systems\n- Fine-grained control over consumption logic\n\n## Error Handling Patterns\n\n### Producer Error Handling\n\n```java\nproducer.send(record, (metadata, exception) -> {\n    if (exception != null) {\n        if (exception instanceof RetriableException) {\n            // Automatic retry by producer\n            logger.warn(\"Retriable error: {}\", exception.getMessage());\n        } else {\n            // Non-retriable - handle explicitly\n            logger.error(\"Failed to send: {}\", exception.getMessage());\n            // Dead letter queue, alert, etc.\n        }\n    } else {\n        logger.info(\"Sent to partition {} offset {}\",\n            metadata.partition(), metadata.offset());\n    }\n});\n```\n\n### Consumer Error Handling\n\n```java\nwhile (true) {\n    ConsumerRecords<String, String> records = consumer.poll(Duration.ofMillis(100));\n\n    for (ConsumerRecord<String, String> record : records) {\n        try {\n            processRecord(record);\n        } catch (TransientException e) {\n            // Retry with backoff\n            retryWithBackoff(record);\n        } catch (PermanentException e) {\n            // Send to DLQ\n            sendToDeadLetterQueue(record, e);\n        }\n    }\n\n    consumer.commitSync(); // Commit after successful processing\n}\n```\n\n## Multi-Language Support\n\n### Python\n\nSee `scripts/python_producer.py` and `scripts/python_consumer.py` for working examples using `confluent-kafka-python`.\n\n**Quick start:**\n\n```python\nfrom confluent_kafka import Producer, Consumer\n\n# Producer\nproducer = Producer({''bootstrap.servers'': ''localhost:9092''})\nproducer.produce(''topic'', key=''key'', value=''value'')\nproducer.flush()\n\n# Consumer\nconsumer = Consumer({\n    ''bootstrap.servers'': ''localhost:9092'',\n    ''group.id'': ''my-group'',\n    ''auto.offset.reset'': ''earliest''\n})\nconsumer.subscribe([''topic''])\n\nwhile True:\n    msg = consumer.poll(1.0)\n    if msg and not msg.error():\n        print(f''Received: {msg.value().decode(\"utf-8\")}'')\n```\n\n### Node.js\n\nSee `scripts/nodejs_producer.js` and `scripts/nodejs_consumer.js` for working examples using `kafkajs`.\n\n**Quick start:**\n\n```javascript\nconst { Kafka } = require(''kafkajs'');\n\nconst kafka = new Kafka({ brokers: [''localhost:9092''] });\n\n// Producer\nconst producer = kafka.producer();\nawait producer.connect();\nawait producer.send({\n  topic: ''topic'',\n  messages: [{ key: ''key'', value: ''value'' }]\n});\n\n// Consumer\nconst consumer = kafka.consumer({ groupId: ''my-group'' });\nawait consumer.connect();\nawait consumer.subscribe({ topic: ''topic'' });\nawait consumer.run({\n  eachMessage: async ({ message }) => {\n    console.log(message.value.toString());\n  }\n});\n```\n\n## Common Patterns and Anti-Patterns\n\n### ✅ Best Practices\n\n1. **Always set `acks=all`** for producers in production\n2. **Use consumer groups** for scalable consumption\n3. **Disable auto-commit** for at-least-once or exactly-once semantics\n4. **Set appropriate `retention.ms`** based on replay requirements\n5. **Monitor consumer lag** to detect processing bottlenecks\n6. **Use compression** (`lz4` or `snappy`) to reduce network bandwidth\n7. **Configure `min.insync.replicas=2`** with `replication-factor=3`\n\n### ❌ Anti-Patterns\n\n1. **Creating too many topics** - Use partitions for parallelism, not topics\n2. **Small batch sizes** - Reduces throughput; increase `batch.size` and `linger.ms`\n3. **Synchronous sends** without batching - Kills performance\n4. **Auto-commit without error handling** - Can lead to message loss\n5. **Not monitoring consumer lag** - Silent degradation\n6. **Single partition topics** - No parallelism or load balancing\n7. **Hardcoding broker addresses** - Use DNS or service discovery\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Producer Issues\n\n**Slow throughput:**\n- Increase `batch.size` and `linger.ms`\n- Enable compression\n- Check network latency to brokers\n- Increase `buffer.memory`\n\n**Messages not arriving:**\n- Check producer error callbacks\n- Verify topic exists and is accessible\n- Check broker logs for errors\n- Verify `acks` configuration\n\n### Consumer Issues\n\n**High lag:**\n- Increase consumer instances (up to partition count)\n- Optimize processing logic\n- Increase `max.poll.records` if processing is fast\n- Check for rebalancing issues\n\n**Rebalancing storms:**\n- Increase `max.poll.interval.ms`\n- Reduce processing time per batch\n- Decrease `max.poll.records`\n- Check session timeout settings\n\n## Reference Files\n\nFor detailed implementation guidance:\n\n- **[STREAMS_GUIDE.md](references/STREAMS_GUIDE.md)** - Kafka Streams API, windowing, joins, state stores\n- **[CONNECT_GUIDE.md](references/CONNECT_GUIDE.md)** - Kafka Connect, source/sink connectors, REST API\n- **[OPERATIONS_GUIDE.md](references/OPERATIONS_GUIDE.md)** - Production deployment, monitoring, disaster recovery\n- **[SCHEMA_MANAGEMENT.md](references/SCHEMA_MANAGEMENT.md)** - Schema Registry, Avro, schema evolution\n\n## Script Directory\n\nAll scripts are tested and ready to use:\n\n- `simple_producer.java` - Basic producer with error handling\n- `simple_consumer.java` - Basic consumer with manual commit\n- `transactional_producer.java` - Exactly-once semantics\n- `word_count_streams.java` - Kafka Streams word count\n- `source_connector.java` - Custom Kafka Connect source connector\n- `python_producer.py` - Python producer example\n- `python_consumer.py` - Python consumer example\n- `nodejs_producer.js` - Node.js producer example\n- `nodejs_consumer.js` - Node.js consumer example\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-06T07:20:38.457Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Distributed System Agents needing scalable event-driven architecture with Apache Kafka","zh":"非常适合需要可扩展的事件驱动架构和Apache Kafka的分布式系统代理","ja":"Apache Kafkaを使用したスケーラブルなイベント駆動型アーキテクチャを必要とする分散システムエージェントに最適","ko":"Apache Kafka를 사용하는 확장 가능한 이벤트 驱动 아키텍처가 필요한 분산 시스템 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Sistemas Distribuidos que necesitan una arquitectura de eventos escalable con Apache Kafka","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de systèmes distribués nécessitant une architecture d''événements évolutives avec Apache Kafka","de":"Perfekt für ver